  "Question": "When \\(x\\) is added to both the numerator and the denominator of the fraction \\(\\frac{a}{b},\\) \\(a\\ne b,\\) \\(b\\ne0,\\) the value of the fraction is changed to \\(\\frac{c}{d}.\\) Then \\(x\\) equals:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(\\dfrac1{c-d}\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\dfrac{ad-bc}{c-d}\\)",
    "C": "\\(\\dfrac{ad-bc}{c+d}\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\dfrac{bc-ad}{c-d}\\)",
    "E": "\\(\\dfrac{bc-ad}{c+d}\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
